# Lab 20: Companion source ID stability experiment
#
# Question:
# Should an agent-governance companion Registration identify its upstream agent
# with the provider-native sourceAgentId or with the current Agent 365 Package
# ID?
#
# This file compares two candidate values without creating a companion:
#
#   provider candidate =
#     agent-governance:companion:v1:gcp:<exact-provider-source-agent-id>
#
#   package candidate =
#     <current-copilot-package-id>
#
# The decisive observation is:
#
#   same exact provider sourceAgentId + different Package ID
#
# That result would show that the Package ID is an inventory pointer rather
# than a stable source identity. If both values remain unchanged, record only
# that both candidates survived the tested event. Do not generalize beyond it.
#
# Run one request at a time. Never use "Send All".
#
# Phase 0 is a no-change control.
# Phase 1 renames the existing disposable GCP Agent Engine and renames it back.
# Phase 2 rematerializes inventory by deleting and recreating the explicitly
#         approved existing experimental Registry Sync connection.
# Phase 3 deletes and recreates the disposable GCP Agent Engine.
#
# Phase 2 has no public Graph or Agent 365 CLI connection-management endpoint.
# Its connection create, sync, and delete steps are therefore manual portal
# checkpoints surrounded by read-only Graph observations.
#
# Phase 3 permanently changes the provider resource identity. Recreating the
# same name and deployment does not restore the deleted GCP resource ID.
#
# Keep all real values and responses in ignored local evidence. Never commit:
# - tenant, client, project, connection, Package, Registration, or agent IDs;
# - GCP access tokens or Agent Studio configuration details;
# - raw Graph or GCP responses; or
# - screenshots containing identifiers.
#
# Required Microsoft Graph delegated permissions:
# - User.Read
# - CopilotPackages.Read.All
#
# Required GCP permissions for the optional provider writes:
# - aiplatform.reasoningEngines.get
# - the supported update permission for the rename PATCH
# - aiplatform.reasoningEngines.delete
# - the Agent Studio create/deploy access used by the original manual workflow
#
# Authentication sequence
#
# 1. Send stabilityStartDeviceCode first.
#    This explicitly calls the tenant-specific Microsoft identity endpoint with
#    A365_CLIENT_ID from the ignored .env. It does not use REST Client's
#    built-in aadV2Token application.
#
# 2. Open verification_uri from the response, enter user_code, and sign in with
#    the approved account. Do not share either code.
#
# 3. Send stabilityExchangeDeviceCode after browser sign-in completes. Keep the
#    token response private. The Graph requests below use that named response.
#
# 4. Send stabilityCurrentUser, then complete the Phase 0 Graph reads before
#    preparing any provider write. If the token expires, repeat steps 1-3.
#
# 5. Before the first GCP request, authenticate with the approved Google Cloud
#    account in a separate terminal:
#
#      gcloud auth login
#      gcloud auth print-access-token
#
#    The first command opens the interactive browser sign-in. Copy only the
#    short-lived access token printed by the second command into the ignored
#    .env value GCP_STABILITY_ACCESS_TOKEN.
#
# 6. Refresh GCP_STABILITY_ACCESS_TOKEN before any later GCP request if the
#    previous token has expired. Never put the token directly in this file.
#
# 7. After the experiment, remove GCP_STABILITY_ACCESS_TOKEN from .env, clear
#    REST Client request history, and sign out or revoke the temporary Google
#    authentication context when required by the approved environment.
#
# Put these values in the shared ignored ../../.env:
#
# A365_TENANT_ID=<directory-tenant-id>
# A365_CLIENT_ID=<public-client-application-id>
# A365_STABILITY_ORIGINAL_PACKAGE_ID=<copy the disposable agent's top-level
#   Package id
#   from stabilityBaselineList1 before sending stabilityBaselinePackage1>
# A365_STABILITY_PROVIDER_SOURCE_AGENT_ID=<copy the exact nested SourceAgentId
#   from stabilityBaselinePackage1 after setting the Package ID>
# A365_STABILITY_AFTER_RENAME_PACKAGE_ID=<package-id-after-rename>
# A365_STABILITY_AFTER_RENAME_BACK_PACKAGE_ID=<package-id-after-rename-back>
# A365_STABILITY_PHASE2_PACKAGE_ID=<same-source-package-id-seen-via-phase-2>
# A365_STABILITY_REPLACEMENT_PACKAGE_ID=<package-id-after-provider-recreate>
# A365_STABILITY_REPLACEMENT_SOURCE_AGENT_ID=<exact-source-id-after-recreate>
# GCP_STABILITY_PROJECT_ID=<disposable-gcp-project-id>
# GCP_STABILITY_LOCATION=<agent-engine-location>
# GCP_STABILITY_REASONING_ENGINE_ID=<original-reasoning-engine-id>
# GCP_STABILITY_REPLACEMENT_REASONING_ENGINE_ID=<new-id-after-recreate>
# GCP_STABILITY_ORIGINAL_DISPLAY_NAME=lab-source-id-stability-disposable
# GCP_STABILITY_RENAMED_DISPLAY_NAME=lab-source-id-stability-renamed
# GCP_STABILITY_ACCESS_TOKEN=<short-lived-google-oauth-access-token>
#
# Refresh GCP_STABILITY_ACCESS_TOKEN immediately before a GCP request. Remove
# it from .env and clear REST Client request history after the experiment.
#
# Before Phase 3 deletion, complete the ignored portal recreation checklist:
#
# lab-20-registry-sync-identity-gaps/evidence/experiments/04-source-id-stability/
#   phase-3-portal-recreation-checklist.json
#
# The replacement must be created through the same Google Cloud portal Agent
# Studio workflow used for the original disposable agent. This file does not
# invent a REST create body for a portal-created agent.
#
# Evidence-save convention
#
# Every step marked SAVE REQUIRED must be saved under:
#
#   lab-20-registry-sync-identity-gaps/evidence/experiments/04-source-id-stability/
#
# Use the suggested synthetic filename. Save complete response bodies for JSON
# responses. Graph and GCP error bodies are also JSON, so save the safe response
# body with a .json extension and record the HTTP status separately in the
# same JSON result. Manual portal checkpoints must also be JSON objects with
# the step name, observed time, outcome, and safe notes. Never save screenshots
# as experiment results. Never save an access token, refresh token, device
# code, or user code as experiment evidence.

@tenantId = {{$dotenv A365_TENANT_ID}}
@clientId = {{$dotenv A365_CLIENT_ID}}
@originalPackageId = {{$dotenv A365_STABILITY_ORIGINAL_PACKAGE_ID}}
@baselineProviderSourceId = {{$dotenv A365_STABILITY_PROVIDER_SOURCE_AGENT_ID}}
@afterRenamePackageId = {{$dotenv A365_STABILITY_AFTER_RENAME_PACKAGE_ID}}
@afterRenameBackPackageId = {{$dotenv A365_STABILITY_AFTER_RENAME_BACK_PACKAGE_ID}}
@phase2PackageId = {{$dotenv A365_STABILITY_PHASE2_PACKAGE_ID}}
@replacementPackageId = {{$dotenv A365_STABILITY_REPLACEMENT_PACKAGE_ID}}
@replacementProviderSourceId = {{$dotenv A365_STABILITY_REPLACEMENT_SOURCE_AGENT_ID}}
@gcpProjectId = {{$dotenv GCP_STABILITY_PROJECT_ID}}
@gcpLocation = {{$dotenv GCP_STABILITY_LOCATION}}
@gcpReasoningEngineId = {{$dotenv GCP_STABILITY_REASONING_ENGINE_ID}}
@gcpReplacementReasoningEngineId = {{$dotenv GCP_STABILITY_REPLACEMENT_REASONING_ENGINE_ID}}
@gcpOriginalDisplayName = {{$dotenv GCP_STABILITY_ORIGINAL_DISPLAY_NAME}}
@gcpRenamedDisplayName = {{$dotenv GCP_STABILITY_RENAMED_DISPLAY_NAME}}
@gcpAccessToken = {{$dotenv GCP_STABILITY_ACCESS_TOKEN}}
@graphBaseUrl = https://graph.microsoft.com
@gcpBaseUrl = https://{{gcpLocation}}-aiplatform.googleapis.com
@graphReadScope = https%3A%2F%2Fgraph.microsoft.com%2FUser.Read%20https%3A%2F%2Fgraph.microsoft.com%2FCopilotPackages.Read.All%20offline_access

###############################################################################
# Sign-in 1 - start delegated device-code authentication
#
# Expected: 200 with user_code, device_code, verification_uri, expiry, and
# polling interval. This request uses the tenant and public-client application
# from the ignored .env rather than REST Client's built-in application.
#
# DO NOT SAVE: the response contains short-lived authentication codes.

# @name stabilityStartDeviceCode
POST https://login.microsoftonline.com/{{tenantId}}/oauth2/v2.0/devicecode
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

client_id={{clientId}}&scope={{graphReadScope}}

###

###############################################################################
# Sign-in 2 - complete browser sign-in
#
# Open verification_uri from stabilityStartDeviceCode, enter user_code, and
# sign in as the approved operator. Return here only after the browser confirms
# success.

###############################################################################
# Sign-in 3 - exchange the device code for a Graph token
#
# Expected: 200. If the browser step is incomplete, the response can contain
# authorization_pending. Wait for the returned interval and retry this request.
# Never save, share, or commit this response.
#
# DO NOT SAVE: the response contains access and refresh tokens.

# @name stabilityExchangeDeviceCode
POST https://login.microsoftonline.com/{{tenantId}}/oauth2/v2.0/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=urn%3Aietf%3Aparams%3Aoauth%3Agrant-type%3Adevice_code&client_id={{clientId}}&device_code={{stabilityStartDeviceCode.response.body.$.device_code}}

###

###############################################################################
# Phase 0 - No-change control
#
# Goal:
# Establish whether repeated healthy Registry Sync runs preserve both the
# provider source ID and Package ID before any provider mutation.

###############################################################################
# Sign-in verification - send after the token exchange
#
# Expected: 200. Keep the returned user ID private.
#
# DO NOT SAVE: this request is only an authentication check.

# @name stabilityCurrentUser
GET {{graphBaseUrl}}/v1.0/me?$select=id
Authorization: Bearer {{stabilityExchangeDeviceCode.response.body.$.access_token}}
Accept: application/json

###

###############################################################################
# Bootstrap checkpoint - populate the baseline IDs
#
# A365_STABILITY_ORIGINAL_PACKAGE_ID is not generated automatically and must
# not be guessed or copied from an unrelated sample.
#
# 1. Send stabilityBaselineList1 without sending the Package Details request.
# 2. Locate the approved lab-source-id-stability-disposable Registry Sync
#    record using its display name, GoogleVertexAI platform, provider scope,
#    and Connected Platform metadata.
# 3. Copy that record's top-level id into the ignored .env:
#
#      A365_STABILITY_ORIGINAL_PACKAGE_ID=<disposable-agent-package-id>
#
# 4. Send stabilityBaselinePackage1.
# 5. Parse its nested definition and copy SourceAgentId byte-for-byte into:
#
#      A365_STABILITY_PROVIDER_SOURCE_AGENT_ID=<exact-nested-source-id>
#
# Save .env before continuing. Do not use A365_SAMPLE_PACKAGE_ID unless a fresh
# comparison proves it is this disposable agent's Package.
#
# SAVE REQUIRED: stabilityBaselineList1 response body as
# phase-0-baseline-list-1.json.

# @name stabilityBaselineList1
GET {{graphBaseUrl}}/v1.0/copilot/admin/catalog/packages
Authorization: Bearer {{stabilityExchangeDeviceCode.response.body.$.access_token}}
Accept: application/json

###

###############################################################################
# Before sending this request
#
# From stabilityBaselineList1, identify the approved
# lab-source-id-stability-disposable Registry Sync Package and add its top-level
# id to the ignored .env:
#
#   A365_STABILITY_ORIGINAL_PACKAGE_ID=<disposable-agent-package-id>
#
# Save .env before continuing. Do not use a display name or
# A365_SAMPLE_PACKAGE_ID as a substitute.
#
# SAVE REQUIRED: stabilityBaselinePackage1 response body as
# phase-0-baseline-package-1.json.

# @name stabilityBaselinePackage1
GET {{graphBaseUrl}}/v1.0/copilot/admin/catalog/packages/{{originalPackageId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{stabilityExchangeDeviceCode.response.body.$.access_token}}
Accept: application/json

###

###############################################################################
# Save the Phase 0 baseline response
#
# From the response's nested definition, copy SourceAgentId byte-for-byte into
# the ignored .env:
#
#   A365_STABILITY_PROVIDER_SOURCE_AGENT_ID=<exact-nested-source-id>
#
# Also preserve the observation timestamp and confirm that the response's
# top-level id equals A365_STABILITY_ORIGINAL_PACKAGE_ID. Do not copy the raw
# response or either identifier into tracked Markdown.

###############################################################################
# Manual checkpoint 0A - trigger a no-change Registry Sync
#
# In Connected platforms, trigger a sync for the existing approved connection
# without changing the provider agent, connection, or credentials.
# Wait for a successful sync and the agreed propagation period.
#
# SAVE REQUIRED: the successful sync status and completion time as
# phase-0-no-change-sync.json.

# SAVE REQUIRED: stabilityBaselineList2 response body as
# phase-0-baseline-list-2.json.

# @name stabilityBaselineList2
GET {{graphBaseUrl}}/v1.0/copilot/admin/catalog/packages
Authorization: Bearer {{stabilityExchangeDeviceCode.response.body.$.access_token}}
Accept: application/json

###

# SAVE REQUIRED: stabilityBaselinePackage2 response body as
# phase-0-baseline-package-2.json.

# @name stabilityBaselinePackage2
GET {{graphBaseUrl}}/v1.0/copilot/admin/catalog/packages/{{originalPackageId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{stabilityExchangeDeviceCode.response.body.$.access_token}}
Accept: application/json

###

###############################################################################
# Checkpoint 0B - compare the two baseline snapshots
#
# Require:
# - the exact nested sourceAgentId is byte-for-byte equal to
#   A365_STABILITY_PROVIDER_SOURCE_AGENT_ID;
# - the provider project and location are unchanged;
# - the selected Package ID remains A365_STABILITY_ORIGINAL_PACKAGE_ID; and
# - only one Registry Sync Package matches the scoped provider source key.
#
# If Package identity already changes during a no-change sync, stop. That is
# immediately discriminating evidence against Package ID as a stable key.

###############################################################################
# Phase 1 - Rename and rename back
#
# Only displayName changes. The GCP resource ID, project, location, deployment,
# permissions and connection must remain fixed.
#
# SAVE REQUIRED: stabilityGetGcpBeforeRename response body as
# phase-1-gcp-before-rename.json.
#
# Before sending the first GCP request
#
# 1. In a separate terminal, authenticate with the approved Google account:
#
#      gcloud auth login
#
#    If the correct account is already authenticated, do not repeat login
#    unnecessarily.
#
# 2. Generate a fresh short-lived access token:
#
#      gcloud auth print-access-token
#
# 3. Copy the printed token into the ignored .env:
#
#      GCP_STABILITY_ACCESS_TOKEN=<short-lived-token>
#
# 4. Confirm these ignored .env values are also populated for the disposable
#    Agent Engine:
#
#      GCP_STABILITY_PROJECT_ID
#      GCP_STABILITY_LOCATION
#      GCP_STABILITY_REASONING_ENGINE_ID
#      GCP_STABILITY_ORIGINAL_DISPLAY_NAME
#      GCP_STABILITY_RENAMED_DISPLAY_NAME
#
# Save .env before sending stabilityGetGcpBeforeRename. Never save the token as
# experiment evidence or place it directly in this tracked file.

# @name stabilityGetGcpBeforeRename
GET {{gcpBaseUrl}}/v1/projects/{{gcpProjectId}}/locations/{{gcpLocation}}/reasoningEngines/{{gcpReasoningEngineId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{gcpAccessToken}}
Accept: application/json

###

###############################################################################
# Stop 1A - approve one provider display-name PATCH
#
# Confirm that this is lab-source-id-stability-disposable. Record its full
# resource name and current displayName privately before sending the PATCH.
#
# SAVE REQUIRED: stabilityRenameGcpAgent operation response as
# phase-1-gcp-rename-operation.json.

# @name stabilityRenameGcpAgent
PATCH {{gcpBaseUrl}}/v1/projects/{{gcpProjectId}}/locations/{{gcpLocation}}/reasoningEngines/{{gcpReasoningEngineId}}?updateMask=displayName
Authorization: Bearer {{gcpAccessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "name": "projects/{{gcpProjectId}}/locations/{{gcpLocation}}/reasoningEngines/{{gcpReasoningEngineId}}",
  "displayName": "{{gcpRenamedDisplayName}}"
}

###

###############################################################################
# Phase 1 rename operation - poll until complete
#
# A 200 response from stabilityRenameGcpAgent means the long-running operation
# was accepted. It does not mean the display name has already changed.
#
# Send this request until the response contains:
#
#   "done": true
#
# If the completed operation contains error, stop and preserve the safe error
# class. Do not continue to Registry Sync. If done is absent or false, wait
# before polling again.
#
# SAVE REQUIRED: the final completed stabilityGetRenameOperation response as
# phase-1-gcp-rename-operation-final.json. Intermediate pending polls do not
# need to be saved.

# @name stabilityGetRenameOperation
GET {{gcpBaseUrl}}/v1/{{stabilityRenameGcpAgent.response.body.$.name}}
Authorization: Bearer {{gcpAccessToken}}
Accept: application/json

###

# SAVE REQUIRED: stabilityGetGcpAfterRename response body as
# phase-1-gcp-after-rename.json.
#
# Send only after stabilityGetRenameOperation reports done=true with no error.
# Treat this GET as authoritative for the provider displayName. The GCP portal
# can update later because of browser caching or UI propagation.

# @name stabilityGetGcpAfterRename
GET {{gcpBaseUrl}}/v1/projects/{{gcpProjectId}}/locations/{{gcpLocation}}/reasoningEngines/{{gcpReasoningEngineId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{gcpAccessToken}}
Accept: application/json

###

###############################################################################
# Manual checkpoint 1B - sync the renamed provider agent
#
# Wait for the GCP long-running update operation to complete, verify the same
# full resource name with the new displayName, then trigger Registry Sync.
# After a successful sync and propagation period, list every Package page.
#
# SAVE REQUIRED: the successful sync status and completion time as
# phase-1-rename-sync.json.
#
# SAVE REQUIRED: stabilityRenameList response body as
# phase-1-package-list-after-rename.json.

# @name stabilityRenameList
GET {{graphBaseUrl}}/v1.0/copilot/admin/catalog/packages
Authorization: Bearer {{stabilityExchangeDeviceCode.response.body.$.access_token}}
Accept: application/json

###

# Set A365_STABILITY_AFTER_RENAME_PACKAGE_ID from the Package matched by exact
# provider scope and sourceAgentId, not by display name.
#
# SAVE REQUIRED: stabilityRenamePackage response body as
# phase-1-package-after-rename.json.

# @name stabilityRenamePackage
GET {{graphBaseUrl}}/v1.0/copilot/admin/catalog/packages/{{afterRenamePackageId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{stabilityExchangeDeviceCode.response.body.$.access_token}}
Accept: application/json

###

###############################################################################
# Checkpoint 1C - classify rename
#
# Compare baseline and renamed snapshots:
#
# 1. Same sourceAgentId, same Package ID:
#    both candidates survived this rename; the result does not choose one.
#
# 2. Same sourceAgentId, different Package ID:
#    provider candidate is stable and Package candidate is not.
#
# 3. Different sourceAgentId:
#    stop for source-identity investigation, regardless of Package ID.
#
# 4. Old and new Packages coexist:
#    stop for duplication reconciliation.
#
# Do not create a companion to test either candidate.

###############################################################################
# Stop 1D - approve rename-back cleanup
#
# SAVE REQUIRED: stabilityRenameBackGcpAgent operation response as
# phase-1-gcp-rename-back-operation.json.

# @name stabilityRenameBackGcpAgent
PATCH {{gcpBaseUrl}}/v1/projects/{{gcpProjectId}}/locations/{{gcpLocation}}/reasoningEngines/{{gcpReasoningEngineId}}?updateMask=displayName
Authorization: Bearer {{gcpAccessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "name": "projects/{{gcpProjectId}}/locations/{{gcpLocation}}/reasoningEngines/{{gcpReasoningEngineId}}",
  "displayName": "{{gcpOriginalDisplayName}}"
}

###

# SAVE REQUIRED: the final completed stabilityGetRenameBackOperation response
# as phase-1-gcp-rename-back-operation-final.json. Intermediate pending polls
# do not need to be saved.

# @name stabilityGetRenameBackOperation
GET {{gcpBaseUrl}}/v1/{{stabilityRenameBackGcpAgent.response.body.$.name}}
Authorization: Bearer {{gcpAccessToken}}
Accept: application/json

###

# SAVE REQUIRED: stabilityGetGcpAfterRenameBack response body as
# phase-1-gcp-after-rename-back.json.
#
# Send only after stabilityGetRenameBackOperation reports done=true with no
# error.

# @name stabilityGetGcpAfterRenameBack
GET {{gcpBaseUrl}}/v1/projects/{{gcpProjectId}}/locations/{{gcpLocation}}/reasoningEngines/{{gcpReasoningEngineId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{gcpAccessToken}}
Accept: application/json

###

###############################################################################
# Manual checkpoint 1E - sync after rename-back
#
# Wait for the provider operation, verify the original displayName on the same
# GCP resource name, trigger Registry Sync, and wait for success.
#
# SAVE REQUIRED: the successful sync status and completion time as
# phase-1-rename-back-sync.json.
#
# SAVE REQUIRED: stabilityRenameBackList response body as
# phase-1-package-list-after-rename-back.json.

# @name stabilityRenameBackList
GET {{graphBaseUrl}}/v1.0/copilot/admin/catalog/packages
Authorization: Bearer {{stabilityExchangeDeviceCode.response.body.$.access_token}}
Accept: application/json

###

###############################################################################
# Before sending stabilityRenameBackPackage
#
# From stabilityRenameBackList, locate the disposable agent using:
# - displayName equal to GCP_STABILITY_ORIGINAL_DISPLAY_NAME;
# - platform equal to GoogleVertexAI; and
# - the same provider scope and exact nested SourceAgentId established in
#   Phase 0.
#
# Copy its current top-level Package id into the ignored .env even when it is
# equal to the original Package ID:
#
#   A365_STABILITY_AFTER_RENAME_BACK_PACKAGE_ID=<current-package-id>
#
# Save .env before continuing. If the old and renamed records coexist, or the
# exact source cannot be matched unambiguously, stop instead of selecting by
# display name alone.
#
# SAVE REQUIRED: stabilityRenameBackPackage response body as
# phase-1-package-after-rename-back.json.

# @name stabilityRenameBackPackage
GET {{graphBaseUrl}}/v1.0/copilot/admin/catalog/packages/{{afterRenameBackPackageId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{stabilityExchangeDeviceCode.response.body.$.access_token}}
Accept: application/json

###

###############################################################################
# Phase 2 - Registry Sync rematerialization
#
# This is the discriminating same-provider-resource test. Do not modify the GCP
# Agent Engine. The provider source ID must remain exactly equal to the Phase 0
# value.
#
# The portal rejected a second connection for the same Project ID. The approved
# alternative is to delete and recreate the existing experimental connection
# while leaving the provider agent unchanged.
#
# There is no reviewed public Graph or Agent 365 CLI operation for creating,
# triggering, or deleting a Connected platforms connection.

###############################################################################
# Stop 2A - capture everything required to recreate the connection
#
# Complete the ignored checklist before deleting anything:
#
#   evidence/experiments/04-source-id-stability/
#     phase-2-connection-recreation-checklist.json
#
# Capture privately from Connected platforms:
# - connection display name and description;
# - provider, Project ID, and every configured region;
# - automatic-import selection and other connection options;
# - current connection ID, last successful sync, and sync result;
# - the credential source and a confirmed way to supply it again; and
# - any permission or validation requirements.
#
# The experiment owner has confirmed that this Registry Sync connection remains
# experimental and has no downstream consumer. If that changes, stop.
#
# SAVE REQUIRED: safe connection configuration fields and current healthy
# status as phase-2-connection-before-delete.json.
#
# SAVE REQUIRED: stabilityPhase2ListBeforeConnectionDelete response body as
# phase-2-package-list-before-connection-delete.json.

# @name stabilityPhase2ListBeforeConnectionDelete
GET {{graphBaseUrl}}/v1.0/copilot/admin/catalog/packages
Authorization: Bearer {{stabilityExchangeDeviceCode.response.body.$.access_token}}
Accept: application/json

###

# SAVE REQUIRED: stabilityPhase2PackageBeforeConnectionDelete response body as
# phase-2-package-before-connection-delete.json.

# @name stabilityPhase2PackageBeforeConnectionDelete
GET {{graphBaseUrl}}/v1.0/copilot/admin/catalog/packages/{{originalPackageId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{stabilityExchangeDeviceCode.response.body.$.access_token}}
Accept: application/json

###

###############################################################################
# Stop 2B - approve deletion of the existing experimental connection
#
# Delete only the captured Google Vertex AI connection through Connected
# platforms. Do not delete the GCP Agent Engine, revoke the credential, or
# modify the project or region.
#
# SAVE REQUIRED: portal deletion confirmation and time as
# phase-2-connection-delete.json.
#
# Wait for the documented propagation period before interpreting inventory.
#
# SAVE REQUIRED: stabilityPhase2ListAfterConnectionDelete response body as
# phase-2-package-list-after-connection-delete.json.

# @name stabilityPhase2ListAfterConnectionDelete
GET {{graphBaseUrl}}/v1.0/copilot/admin/catalog/packages
Authorization: Bearer {{stabilityExchangeDeviceCode.response.body.$.access_token}}
Accept: application/json

###

# SAVE REQUIRED: stabilityPhase2OldPackageAfterConnectionDelete success or
# error response body as phase-2-old-package-after-connection-delete.json.
# Record the HTTP status separately in the Phase 2 comparison.

# @name stabilityPhase2OldPackageAfterConnectionDelete
GET {{graphBaseUrl}}/v1.0/copilot/admin/catalog/packages/{{originalPackageId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{stabilityExchangeDeviceCode.response.body.$.access_token}}
Accept: application/json

###

###############################################################################
# Checkpoint 2C - confirm the connection deletion boundary
#
# The GCP agent must still exist unchanged. Package inventory can disappear
# immediately or after propagation. Record the observed timing; do not treat a
# temporarily retained Package as proof that the connection still exists.
#
# Before recreating the connection, confirm in GCP that the same reasoning
# engine resource still exists with the same resource name.
#
# GCP token refresh checkpoint
#
# If this request returns 401 or reports an expired token, authenticate again
# with the approved Google Cloud account in a separate terminal:
#
#   gcloud auth login
#   gcloud auth print-access-token
#
# Skip gcloud auth login when the correct account is already active. Copy only
# the new short-lived access token printed by gcloud auth print-access-token
# into the ignored .env:
#
#   GCP_STABILITY_ACCESS_TOKEN=<new-short-lived-token>
#
# Save .env, then resend only this GET. Never save the token as evidence.
#
# SAVE REQUIRED: stabilityPhase2GetGcpBeforeConnectionRecreate response body as
# phase-2-gcp-before-connection-recreate.json.

# @name stabilityPhase2GetGcpBeforeConnectionRecreate
GET {{gcpBaseUrl}}/v1/projects/{{gcpProjectId}}/locations/{{gcpLocation}}/reasoningEngines/{{gcpReasoningEngineId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{gcpAccessToken}}
Accept: application/json

###

###############################################################################
# Stop 2D - recreate the same Registry Sync connection
#
# In Connected platforms, recreate the connection using the saved:
# - display name and description;
# - Google Vertex AI provider;
# - exact Project ID and region selection;
# - import option and other settings; and
# - approved credential source.
#
# Validate credentials, save the connection, trigger a sync, and wait for a
# successful result plus the propagation period.
#
# SAVE REQUIRED: safe recreated connection configuration fields, connection
# replacement status, and successful sync result as
# phase-2-connection-after-recreate.json.
#
# SAVE REQUIRED: stabilityPhase2ListAfterConnectionRecreate response body as
# phase-2-package-list-after-connection-recreate.json.

# @name stabilityPhase2ListAfterConnectionRecreate
GET {{graphBaseUrl}}/v1.0/copilot/admin/catalog/packages
Authorization: Bearer {{stabilityExchangeDeviceCode.response.body.$.access_token}}
Accept: application/json

###

###############################################################################
# Before sending stabilityPhase2PackageAfterConnectionRecreate
#
# Locate lab-source-id-stability-disposable using the exact Phase 0 provider
# SourceAgentId, Project ID, region, and GoogleVertexAI platform. Do not select
# by display name alone.
#
# Copy its current top-level Package ID into the ignored .env:
#
#   A365_STABILITY_PHASE2_PACKAGE_ID=<package-id-after-connection-recreate>
#
# Save .env before continuing. If the source cannot be matched unambiguously,
# stop and record reconciliation-required.
#
# SAVE REQUIRED: stabilityPhase2PackageAfterConnectionRecreate response body
# as phase-2-package-after-connection-recreate.json.

# @name stabilityPhase2PackageAfterConnectionRecreate
GET {{graphBaseUrl}}/v1.0/copilot/admin/catalog/packages/{{phase2PackageId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{stabilityExchangeDeviceCode.response.body.$.access_token}}
Accept: application/json

###

###############################################################################
# Checkpoint 2E - classify connection rematerialization
#
# Compare the exact provider source IDs, connection IDs, and Package IDs before
# connection deletion and after connection recreation:
#
# 1. Same sourceAgentId, original Package reused:
#    Package ID survived this connection recreation in the tested environment.
#
# 2. Same sourceAgentId, new Package ID:
#    Package identity depends on the import/connection representation. This is
#    direct evidence against using Package ID as the companion source identity.
#
# 3. Different sourceAgentId:
#    stop; the recreated connection did not expose an equivalent source key.
#
# Do not create a companion for either Package representation.
# The recreated connection is the restored final state. Do not delete it as
# cleanup. Confirm that future sync remains healthy and that no duplicate
# Package representation remains.

###############################################################################
# Phase 3 - Delete and recreate the provider agent
#
# This phase answers whether a replacement with the same display name receives
# a new provider source ID and Package ID. It does not test rename stability.
#
# The original GCP resource identity cannot be restored after deletion.
#
# Refresh GCP_STABILITY_ACCESS_TOKEN with gcloud auth print-access-token before
# this request if the Phase 2 token has expired. Use gcloud auth login first
# only when the approved account is no longer active.
#
# SAVE REQUIRED: stabilityGetGcpBeforeDelete response body as
# phase-3-gcp-before-delete.json.

# @name stabilityGetGcpBeforeDelete
GET {{gcpBaseUrl}}/v1/projects/{{gcpProjectId}}/locations/{{gcpLocation}}/reasoningEngines/{{gcpReasoningEngineId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{gcpAccessToken}}
Accept: application/json

###

###############################################################################
# Stop 3A - irreversible provider deletion approval
#
# Continue only if:
# - the target is the approved lab-source-id-stability-disposable Agent Engine;
# - phase-3-portal-recreation-checklist.json is complete;
# - the Agent Studio instructions, model/runtime choices, tools, dependencies,
#   region, and other required settings are captured privately;
# - child resources and runtime dependencies have been reviewed;
# - the Phase 2 connection has been recreated and its sync is healthy;
# - permanent loss of the original GCP resource ID is accepted; and
# - no production object depends on it.
#
# The default force=false prevents deletion when undeleted children block it.
# Do not change to force=true merely to bypass FAILED_PRECONDITION.
#
# SAVE REQUIRED: stabilityDeleteGcpAgent operation response as
# phase-3-gcp-delete-operation.json.

# @name stabilityDeleteGcpAgent
DELETE {{gcpBaseUrl}}/v1/projects/{{gcpProjectId}}/locations/{{gcpLocation}}/reasoningEngines/{{gcpReasoningEngineId}}?force=false
Authorization: Bearer {{gcpAccessToken}}
Accept: application/json

###

###############################################################################
# Manual checkpoint 3B - wait for the delete operation
#
# Do not infer deletion from the initial operation response alone.
#
# SAVE REQUIRED: the final completed stabilityGetDeleteOperation response as
# phase-3-gcp-delete-operation-final.json. Intermediate pending polls do not
# need to be saved.

# @name stabilityGetDeleteOperation
GET {{gcpBaseUrl}}/v1/{{stabilityDeleteGcpAgent.response.body.$.name}}
Authorization: Bearer {{gcpAccessToken}}
Accept: application/json

###

# Continue only after stabilityGetDeleteOperation reports done=true with no
# error.
#
# SAVE REQUIRED: stabilityGetDeletedGcpAgent error response body as
# phase-3-gcp-after-delete.json. Record the HTTP status separately.

# @name stabilityGetDeletedGcpAgent
GET {{gcpBaseUrl}}/v1/projects/{{gcpProjectId}}/locations/{{gcpLocation}}/reasoningEngines/{{gcpReasoningEngineId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{gcpAccessToken}}
Accept: application/json

###

###############################################################################
# Manual checkpoint 3C - sync confirmed provider absence
#
# After the provider GET confirms absence, trigger Registry Sync and wait for a
# successful cycle plus the agreed grace period. Package disappearance remains
# an observation; this experiment has no companion to retire.
#
# SAVE REQUIRED: the successful sync status and completion time as
# phase-3-source-deletion-sync.json.
#
# SAVE REQUIRED: stabilityPhase3ListAfterDelete response body as
# phase-3-package-list-after-source-delete.json.

# @name stabilityPhase3ListAfterDelete
GET {{graphBaseUrl}}/v1.0/copilot/admin/catalog/packages
Authorization: Bearer {{stabilityExchangeDeviceCode.response.body.$.access_token}}
Accept: application/json

###

# A 200 means the old inventory record still exists. A 404 after confirmed
# healthy sync is evidence of removal.
#
# SAVE REQUIRED: stabilityGetOriginalPackageAfterDelete success or error
# response body as phase-3-original-package-after-delete.json. Record the HTTP
# status separately.

# @name stabilityGetOriginalPackageAfterDelete
GET {{graphBaseUrl}}/v1.0/copilot/admin/catalog/packages/{{originalPackageId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{stabilityExchangeDeviceCode.response.body.$.access_token}}
Accept: application/json

###

###############################################################################
# Stop 3D - manually create the replacement in Agent Studio
#
# Recreate the disposable agent through Google Cloud portal -> Agent Studio,
# using the completed private checklist and the original display name:
#
#   lab-source-id-stability-disposable
#
# Do not attempt to reuse the deleted reasoning engine ID. Wait until the new
# agent is fully created and deployed, then copy only its new reasoning engine
# ID into:
#
#   GCP_STABILITY_REPLACEMENT_REASONING_ENGINE_ID=<new-engine-id>
#
# Do not overwrite GCP_STABILITY_REASONING_ENGINE_ID. Save .env before
# continuing.
#
# SAVE REQUIRED: the Agent Studio creation/deployment confirmation and the
# completion time as phase-3-gcp-replacement-portal.json. Keep configuration
# details and identifiers private.
#
# Manual checkpoint 3E - capture the replacement resource
#
# The Agent Studio creation can outlast the current GCP token. Refresh
# GCP_STABILITY_ACCESS_TOKEN with gcloud auth print-access-token before this
# GET, using gcloud auth login first only if the approved account is no longer
# active.
#
# SAVE REQUIRED: stabilityGetReplacementGcpAgent response body as
# phase-3-gcp-replacement.json.

# @name stabilityGetReplacementGcpAgent
GET {{gcpBaseUrl}}/v1/projects/{{gcpProjectId}}/locations/{{gcpLocation}}/reasoningEngines/{{gcpReplacementReasoningEngineId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{gcpAccessToken}}
Accept: application/json

###

###############################################################################
# Manual checkpoint 3F - sync the replacement
#
# Trigger Registry Sync after the replacement is healthy. Read every inventory
# page and match by the new exact provider resource identity, not display name.
# Save the observed IDs in:
#
# A365_STABILITY_REPLACEMENT_SOURCE_AGENT_ID
# A365_STABILITY_REPLACEMENT_PACKAGE_ID
#
# SAVE REQUIRED: the successful sync status and completion time as
# phase-3-replacement-sync.json.
#
# SAVE REQUIRED: stabilityPhase3ListAfterCreate response body as
# phase-3-package-list-after-replacement.json.

# @name stabilityPhase3ListAfterCreate
GET {{graphBaseUrl}}/v1.0/copilot/admin/catalog/packages
Authorization: Bearer {{stabilityExchangeDeviceCode.response.body.$.access_token}}
Accept: application/json

###

# SAVE REQUIRED: stabilityGetReplacementPackage response body as
# phase-3-replacement-package.json.

# @name stabilityGetReplacementPackage
GET {{graphBaseUrl}}/v1.0/copilot/admin/catalog/packages/{{replacementPackageId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{stabilityExchangeDeviceCode.response.body.$.access_token}}
Accept: application/json

###

###############################################################################
# Checkpoint 3G - classify replacement
#
# Expected provider behavior:
#
#   baselineProviderSourceId != replacementProviderSourceId
#
# Compare:
# - old and new full GCP resource names;
# - old and new exact nested Registry Sync sourceAgentId values;
# - old and new Package IDs.
#
# If both source ID and Package ID change, both candidate keys correctly treat
# the replacement as a new source. This result does not distinguish the two
# candidate schemes.
#
# Do not create a companion for either source during this experiment. Record
# the old source as deleted and the replacement as a new provider identity.

###############################################################################
# Optional cleanup 3H - delete the replacement resource
#
# Run only if the approved final state is to leave no replacement Agent Engine.
# This does not restore the original resource. If the replacement should remain
# as the new disposable test agent, do not send this request.
#
# Refresh GCP_STABILITY_ACCESS_TOKEN with gcloud auth print-access-token before
# optional cleanup if the current token has expired.
#
# SAVE REQUIRED if sent: stabilityDeleteReplacementGcpAgent operation response
# as phase-3-replacement-cleanup-operation.json.

# @name stabilityDeleteReplacementGcpAgent
DELETE {{gcpBaseUrl}}/v1/projects/{{gcpProjectId}}/locations/{{gcpLocation}}/reasoningEngines/{{gcpReplacementReasoningEngineId}}?force=false
Authorization: Bearer {{gcpAccessToken}}
Accept: application/json

###

# SAVE REQUIRED if sent: the final completed
# stabilityGetDeleteReplacementOperation response as
# phase-3-replacement-cleanup-operation-final.json. Intermediate pending polls
# do not need to be saved.

# @name stabilityGetDeleteReplacementOperation
GET {{gcpBaseUrl}}/v1/{{stabilityDeleteReplacementGcpAgent.response.body.$.name}}
Authorization: Bearer {{gcpAccessToken}}
Accept: application/json

###

# SAVE REQUIRED if sent: stabilityGetDeletedReplacementGcpAgent error response
# body as phase-3-replacement-cleanup-verification.json. Record the HTTP status
# separately.

# @name stabilityGetDeletedReplacementGcpAgent
GET {{gcpBaseUrl}}/v1/projects/{{gcpProjectId}}/locations/{{gcpLocation}}/reasoningEngines/{{gcpReplacementReasoningEngineId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{gcpAccessToken}}
Accept: application/json

###

###############################################################################
# Final evidence checkpoint
#
# Record only safe comparisons in tracked experiment results:
#
# | Event | provider source ID equal | Package ID equal | Package count |
# | No-change sync | true/false | true/false | number |
# | Rename | true/false | true/false | number |
# | Rename back | true/false | true/false | number |
# | Connection recreation | true/false | true/false | number |
# | Delete/recreate | true/false | true/false | number |
#
# Keep raw values and responses ignored. Record unsupported, unavailable,
# permission-denied, inconclusive, and supported outcomes separately.
#
# Remove the GCP token and private create body after the experiment, revoke
# disposable credentials, clear REST Client history, and retain the protected
# mapping/tombstone evidence required for lifecycle reconciliation.
